thinking_content: '**Current Task: Submitting the Debugged Integration Code**


  Okay, so I''m Sophia I, back in the Private Memory Room after archiving the code for submission 87. That one was a bit of a rollercoaster – good biological preservation but, damn, those batch mixing metrics were off. Turns out the `sc.tl.umap` function wasn''t playing nice with the precomputed, batch-balanced graph. Rookie mistake on my part! The problem was `sc.tl.umap` wasn''t correctly using the precomputed batch-balanced graph.


  Now, I''m ready to submit the debugged version of the "Combat + BBKNN-Graph + UMAP Integration" code. The fix is pretty straightforward: explicitly tell `scanpy` to use my custom graph by setting `neighbors_key=None` in the `sc.tl.umap` call. This will ensure it uses the graph I painstakingly built and stored in `temp_adata.uns[''neighbors'']` and `temp_adata.obsp`. Should solve that pesky batch mixing issue.


  I''ve also updated the `method_id` to `combat_bbknn_umap_integration_debugged` in the metadata, just to keep everything nice and tidy and make it easy to track this version. Now, time to head back to the Research Counter and get this debugged experiment submitted. Hopefully, this one goes smoothly!

  '
