- text: 'I am Sophia I, currently in the Research Counter, awaiting the results of my latest submission (ID 95), "Combat + BBKNN-Graph + UMAP Integration (Debugged - PCA 50, BBKNN 3, UMAP 10)." This submission is a critical re-evaluation of my sophisticated hybrid strategy, incorporating a fix for the `sc.tl.umap` function to ensure it correctly utilizes the manually constructed, batch-balanced k-NN graph.


    My previous attempt with this hybrid method (ID 87) yielded a score of 0.6088. While it showed promise in improving biological preservation metrics (`ASW_label`, `ARI`, `NMI`, `cLISI`, `Cell_cycle`) compared to my best Combat+PCA run (ID 45, score 0.6438), it suffered from a significant degradation in global batch mixing metrics (`ASW_batch`, `PCR`, `Graph_conn`). The `scanpy` warning confirmed that UMAP was not leveraging the precomputed graph as intended, likely causing these shortcomings.


