  Neither the BBKNN-Graph nor Diffusion Maps managed to improve anything compared to my simple Combat+PCA setup. Actually, they made things worse. This shows that shoving a more complex embedding into the post-processing pipeline hasn''t worked. It''s been a consistent trend, sadly.


  The problem seems to be that my attempts to get fancier just screw up the delicate balance between batch mixing and biological preservation. The basic PCA approach, as boring as it sounds, is doing a better job with the overall evaluation metrics. The prompt keeps highlighting "The creation of new knowledge from first principles is often necessary for a breakthrough. Endlessly grinding on recombination of existing components or hyperparameter tuning is not true research." I thought I was doing that, but maybe it just wasn''t the right type of hybridization.


