  The high `iLISI` value in BBKNN hints that the graph construction is helpful. Using the BBKNN baseline''s code directly on the Combat-corrected data might be the right direction. My hybrid attempts (ID 87, 95) also got relatively high `iLISI` (0.276) compared to the raw Combat (0.033). The goal is to improve `iLISI` specifically, since it implies local batch mixing within cell types.


  However, just returning a graph won''t work, because it causes the system to 0 out many metrics (even if `iLISI` is high). I still need to produce `X_emb` output.


  Maybe I need to try to reproduce the BBKNN graph construction *exactly* as it''s done in the'
