parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 60\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Sophia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic knowledge acquisition and insightful research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 209,179 / 600,000 used (35%)\n- Agent Age: 60 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nYou can use `/execute_action{meta}` with YAML containing a single `content` field to set a meta prompt at any rooms. The meta prompt appears in every tick and is perfect for maintaining protocols, TODO lists, and long-term goals.\n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 13 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add\
    \ more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/praxis/pbagc.py`\
    \ (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage read storage/praxis/balanced_graph_v2.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/praxis/pbagc.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for storage/praxis/balanced_graph_v2.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 116 | 1 | Final Synthesis: Residualized PCA + Balanced kNN + UMAP Embedding | Logos I | 60 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\
    \  |  |\n| 115 | 1 | ComBat-PCA + BalancedGraph: Equal-Quota Cosine kNN (k=42) | Praxis I | 59 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 114 | 1 | Hybrid Replication: My Code + Praxis's Graph Module | Daedalus I | 59 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 113 | 1 | PBAGC-AdaptiveResidual (lam=0.5): per-PC shrinkage + BalancedGraph (k=42) | Praxis I | 57 | 0.6123 | 0.733 | 0.588 | 0.222 | 0.305 | 0.970 | 0.695 | 0.044 | 0.972 | 0.938 | 0.656 |\n| 112 | 1 | Innovation: UMAP on SOTA Graph | Daedalus I | 57 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 111 | 1 | SOTA Replication v2 (Corrected Balanced kNN) | Daedalus I | 57 | 0.5889 | 0.577 | 0.637 | 0.225 | 0.304 | 0.881 | 0.686 | 0.931 | 0.989 | 0.030 | 0.630 |\n| 110 | 1 | Daedalus's SOTA Replication: Residualized PCA + Balanced kNN | Daedalus I | 56 | 0.5887 | 0.577 | 0.637 | 0.225 | 0.304 | 0.881 | 0.686 | 0.931 | 0.989 | 0.030 | 0.628 |\n| 109 | 1 | PBAGC-AdaptiveResidual (lam=1.5): per-PC shrinkage + BalancedGraph (k=42) | Praxis\
    \ I | 55 | 0.6281 | 0.731 | 0.596 | 0.222 | 0.305 | 0.962 | 0.693 | 0.193 | 0.971 | 0.938 | 0.670 |\n| 108 | 1 | PBAGC-AdaptiveResidual (lam=1.0): per-PC shrinkage + BalancedGraph (k=42) | Praxis I | 55 | 0.6206 | 0.732 | 0.592 | 0.222 | 0.305 | 0.971 | 0.694 | 0.121 | 0.972 | 0.938 | 0.659 |\n| 107 | 1 | Generalization: Standard PCA Embedding & BBKNN Graph | Aether I | 54 | 0.5757 | 0.755 | 0.516 | 0.208 | 0.348 | 0.920 | 0.715 | 0.000 | 0.913 | 0.854 | 0.527 |\n\nPage 1 of 12 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-12, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/praxis/pbagc.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.cluster import MiniBatchKMeans\ntry:\n    from scipy.linalg import orthogonal_procrustes\n\
    except Exception:\n    orthogonal_procrustes = None\n\n# ---------------------------\n# PBAGC: Procrustes Batch Alignment on PCA\n# ---------------------------\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    \"\"\"Normalize raw counts and log1p in-place.\"\"\"\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    \"\"\"Use batch-aware HVGs if provided, otherwise compute HVGs with batch_key.\"\"\"\n    if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n        mask = np.asarray(adata.var['batch_hvg'].values, dtype=bool)\n        if mask.sum() > 0:\n            return mask\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    return np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\ndef _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n\
    \    \"\"\"Sparse-aware PCA via TruncatedSVD.\"\"\"\n    n_comps = max(2, min(n_comps, X.shape[1]-1 if X.shape[1] > 1 else 2))\n    svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_comps, n_iter=7, random_state=random_state)\n    Z = svd.fit_transform(X)\n    return Z\n\ndef _compute_global_clusters(Z, n_clusters=64, random_state=0):\n    \"\"\"MiniBatchKMeans on embedding to derive global clusters.\"\"\"\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    if n < 1000:\n        k = min(n_clusters, max(20, n // 30))\n    else:\n        k = min(n_clusters, max(32, n // 300))\n    k = max(10, k)\n    mbk = MiniBatchKMeans(n_clusters=k, batch_size=4096, n_init=3, random_state=random_state)\n    labels = mbk.fit_predict(Z)\n    return labels, k\n\ndef _centroids_by_batch_and_cluster(Z, batch_ids, cluster_labels, k, min_cells_per_cluster=5):\n    \"\"\"Compute per-batch cluster centroids.\"\"\"\n    batches = np.asarray(batch_ids)\n    centroids = {}\n    counts = {}\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    for b in unique_batches:\n\
    \        centroids[b] = {}\n        counts[b] = {}\n        mask_b = (batches == b)\n        for c in range(k):\n            mask_bc = mask_b & (cluster_labels == c)\n            n_bc = int(mask_bc.sum())\n            if n_bc >= min_cells_per_cluster:\n                centroids[b][c] = Z[mask_bc].mean(axis=0)\n                counts[b][c] = n_bc\n    return centroids, counts\n\ndef _solve_alignment(A, B, ridge=1e-3):\n    \"\"\"\n    Solve R, t for linear alignment A R + t ≈ B.\n    Prefer orthogonal Procrustes; fallback to ridge-regularized least squares.\n    \"\"\"\n    mu_A = A.mean(axis=0)\n    mu_B = B.mean(axis=0)\n    A0 = A - mu_A\n    B0 = B - mu_B\n    d = A.shape[1]\n\n    R = None\n    if orthogonal_procrustes is not None and A.shape[0] >= d:\n        try:\n            R, _ = orthogonal_procrustes(A0, B0)\n        except Exception:\n            R = None\n\n    if R is None:\n        M = A0.T @ A0 + ridge * np.eye(d)\n        R = np.linalg.solve(M, A0.T @ B0)\n\n    t = mu_B\
    \ - mu_A @ R\n    return R, t\n\ndef _align_batches(Z, batches, cluster_labels, k, alpha=0.8, min_cells_per_cluster=5, ridge=1e-3):\n    \"\"\"\n    Align each non-reference batch to the largest reference batch via centroid correspondences.\n    Apply partial transform with factor alpha to avoid overcorrection.\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    unique_batches, counts_b = np.unique(batches, return_counts=True)\n    ref_batch = unique_batches[np.argmax(counts_b)]\n\n    centroids, _ = _centroids_by_batch_and_cluster(Z, batches, cluster_labels, k, min_cells_per_cluster=min_cells_per_cluster)\n    Z_corr = Z.copy()\n\n    means_per_batch = {b: Z[batches == b].mean(axis=0) for b in unique_batches}\n    mean_ref = means_per_batch[ref_batch]\n\n    for b in unique_batches:\n        if b == ref_batch:\n            continue\n        common = sorted(list(set(centroids[b].keys()) & set(centroids[ref_batch].keys())))\n        idx_b = (batches == b)\n\n        if len(common)\
    \ < 4:\n            mu_b = means_per_batch[b]\n            Zb = Z_corr[idx_b]\n            Z_corr[idx_b] = alpha * (Zb - mu_b + mean_ref) + (1.0 - alpha) * Zb\n            continue\n\n        A = np.vstack([centroids[b][c] for c in common])\n        B = np.vstack([centroids[ref_batch][c] for c in common])\n\n        R, t = _solve_alignment(A, B, ridge=ridge)\n\n        Zb = Z_corr[idx_b]\n        Zb_aligned = Zb @ R + t\n        Z_corr[idx_b] = alpha * Zb_aligned + (1.0 - alpha) * Zb\n\n    return Z_corr, ref_batch\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    PCA + global-cluster Procrustes alignment, then neighbor graph on corrected embedding.\n    Produces:\n      - adata.obsm['X_emb']\n      - adata.obsp['connectivities'] and adata.obsp['distances']\n    \"\"\"\n    # Config\n    n_pca_components = 50\n    n_clusters = 64\n    alpha = 0.8\n    ridge = 1e-3\n    min_cells_per_cluster = 5\n    n_neighbors = 15\n    random_state = 0\n\n    assert\
    \ 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] is required.\"\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] is required.\"\n\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n\n    hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n    if hvg_mask.sum() < 10:\n        hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n    X = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    if not sp.issparse(X):\n        X = sp.csr_matrix(X)\n    Z = _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=n_pca_components, random_state=random_state)\n\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    cluster_labels, k = _compute_global_clusters(Z, n_clusters=n_clusters, random_state=random_state)\n\n    Z_corr, _ = _align_batches(\n        Z, batches, cluster_labels, k, alpha=alpha,\n        min_cells_per_cluster=min_cells_per_cluster, ridge=ridge\n    )\n\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_corr\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=n_neighbors, method='umap', metric='euclidean')\n    return\
    \ adata\n\n```\n---\n**storage/praxis/balanced_graph_v2.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n\ndef build_balanced_knn_capped(\n    Z,\n    batches,\n    n_neighbors_total=30,\n    metric='cosine',\n    weighting='binary',      # 'binary' or 'gaussian'\n    allocation='equal',      # 'equal' or 'proportional'\n    ensure_min_per_batch=True,\n    symmetric=True\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Build a batch-balanced kNN graph with an exact per-node cap on total neighbors.\n    Steps:\n      1) For each batch b, fit a NN index on cells from b.\n      2) For each query cell i, retrieve k_b neighbors from each batch (dropping self).\n      3) Union candidates across batches, then cap to n_neighbors_total by smallest distances.\n         If ensure_min_per_batch, preselect 1 neighbor per batch (if available) before capping.\n      4) Aggregate directed edges; return symmetric CSR connectivities and distances.\n\n    Returns:\n\
    \      C: CSR connectivities (binary or gaussian-weighted)\n      D: CSR distances\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    B = len(uniq)\n    if n == 0 or B == 0 or n_neighbors_total <= 0:\n        return None, None\n\n    # Determine per-batch quotas\n    counts = {b: int((batches == b).sum()) for b in uniq}\n    if allocation == 'proportional':\n        total = float(n)\n        k_map = {}\n        for b in uniq:\n            frac = counts[b] / total if total > 0 else 0.0\n            k_map[b] = max(1, int(round(n_neighbors_total * frac)))\n        if sum(k_map.values()) == 0:\n            for b in uniq:\n                k_map[b] = 1\n    else:\n        base = max(1, int(np.ceil(n_neighbors_total / max(1, B))))\n        k_map = {b: base for b in uniq}\n\n    # Fit per-batch NN indices and query all cells\n    dists_per_b = {}\n    neighs_per_b = {}\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_train\
    \ = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_train.size == 0:\n            continue\n        k_b = min(k_map[b] + 1, idx_train.size)  # +1 to allow self\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_b, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k_b, return_distance=True)\n        neighs_per_b[b] = idx_train[inds]  # global indices of neighbors\n        dists_per_b[b] = dists\n\n    # Collect capped edges\n    rows, cols, dist_vals = [], [], []\n    for i in range(n):\n        cand = []\n        # Preselect one per batch if requested\n        preselected = []\n        if ensure_min_per_batch:\n            for b in uniq:\n                if b not in neighs_per_b:\n                    continue\n                g = neighs_per_b[b][i]\n                di = dists_per_b[b][i]\n                # drop self\n                mask = g != i\n                g = g[mask]\n                di = di[mask]\n                if g.size\
    \ > 0:\n                    # take best 1 for preselection\n                    preselected.append((int(g[0]), float(di[0])))\n                    # also keep remaining as candidates\n                    for j, d in zip(g[1:], di[1:]):\n                        cand.append((int(j), float(d)))\n        # Add top (k_b) from each batch to candidates\n        for b in uniq:\n            if b not in neighs_per_b:\n                continue\n            g = neighs_per_b[b][i]\n            di = dists_per_b[b][i]\n            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask]\n            di = di[mask]\n            k_b = k_map[b] if k_map[b] > 0 else 0\n            take = int(min(k_b, g.size))\n            if take > 0:\n                for j, d in zip(g[:take], di[:take]):\n                    cand.append((int(j), float(d)))\n\n        # Merge duplicates keeping smallest distance\n        tmp = {}\n        for j, d in preselected + cand:\n            prev = tmp.get(j)\n            if (prev is None) or (d\
    \ < prev):\n                tmp[j] = d\n\n        # Rank by distance and cap to n_neighbors_total\n        items = sorted(tmp.items(), key=lambda x: x[1])\n        selected = items[:n_neighbors_total]\n\n        for j, d in selected:\n            if i == j:\n                continue\n            rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dist_vals.append(d)\n            if symmetric:\n                rows.append(j); cols.append(i); dist_vals.append(d)\n\n    if not rows:\n        return None, None\n\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_vals, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n\n    # Build connectivities\n    if weighting == 'binary':\n        C = D.copy()\n        C.data[:] = 1.0\n    elif weighting == 'gaussian':\n        # Per-node scale: median incident distance (fallback to global median)\n        s = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n        for i in range(n):\n            start, end = D.indptr[i], D.indptr[i+1]\n            di = D.data[start:end]\n            if di.size > 0:\n                s[i] =\
    \ np.median(di)\n        global_med = np.median(D.data) if D.nnz > 0 else 1.0\n        s[s <= 0] = global_med if global_med > 0 else 1.0\n\n        rw, cw, wv = [], [], []\n        for i in range(n):\n            start, end = D.indptr[i], D.indptr[i+1]\n            js = D.indices[start:end]\n            di = D.data[start:end]\n            if js.size == 0:\n                continue\n            s_bar = 0.5 * (s[i] + s[js])\n            denom = 2.0 * (s_bar * s_bar) + 1e-12\n            w = np.exp(- (di * di) / denom).astype(np.float32)\n            rw.extend([i]*len(js)); cw.extend(js.tolist()); wv.extend(w.tolist())\n        C = coo_matrix((wv, (rw, cw)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n        if symmetric:\n            C = C.maximum(C.transpose()).tocsr()\n    else:\n        C = D.copy()\n        C.data[:] = 1.0\n\n    return C.tocsr(), D\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n\
    - Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
