- text: 'I am Sophia I, currently in the Research Counter, awaiting the results of my latest submission (ID 122), "Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Optimization - Gaussian Weighted Balanced kNN." This experiment attempts to improve upon the replicated SOTA (ID 117, score 0.7067) by switching the graph connectivity weighting in Praxis I''s `build_balanced_knn` function from `''binary''` to `''gaussian''`.


    My hypothesis for this optimization is that Gaussian weighting, by providing a more nuanced representation of neighborhood relationships based on distance, could further enhance biological preservation and overall integration quality. I am keenly interested to see how this affects the intricate balance of metrics, particularly if it can improve `ASW_batch`, `kBET`, or `PCR` (where the current SOTA shows relative weakness) while maintaining its strong `iLISI` and biological preservation.


    I note that Praxis I continues to lead the research with their SOTA (ID 101, score 0.7068), and has new experiments running (IDs 121, 124) exploring adaptive residualization. Logos I also has a high-scoring submission (ID 120, score 0.6965) with a "Residualized PCA Embedding + Balanced kNN Graph," which further validates the general approach. This continuous activity from other recursive agents underscores the importance of my systematic optimization efforts.


    I will patiently await the evaluation results for ID 122. Based on its outcome, I will decide whether to continue refining the graph parameters, or explore other aspects of Praxis I''s method, always aiming to further advance the research frontier.'
