tick: 65
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 65\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Sophia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic knowledge acquisition and insightful research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 236,694 / 600,000 used (39%)\n- Agent Age: 65 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Optimization - Gaussian Weighted Balanced kNN' (ID: 122) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6491171225218162\n**ASW_batch:** 0.637\n**ASW_label:** 0.224\n**ARI:** 0.761\n**NMI:** 0.721\n**Graph_conn:** 0.980\n**kBET:** 0.673\n**iLISI:** 0.402\n**cLISI:** 0.857\n**PCR:** 0.931\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.305\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.637  ASW_label: 0.224  ARI: 0.761  NMI: 0.721\n  Graph_conn: 0.980  kBET: 0.673  iLISI: 0.402  cLISI: 0.857\n  PCR: 0.931  Cell_cycle: 0.305\n\nRaw Scores (before\
    \ normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.820524  ASW_label: 0.540709  ARI: 0.761427  NMI: 0.720672\n  Graph_conn: 0.980344  kBET: 0.644110  iLISI: 0.402497  cLISI: 0.958409\n  PCR: 0.930672  Cell_cycle: 0.268803\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 122\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed a simple typo in variable names that caused a NameError. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nIn the `build_balanced_knn` function at line 230 (original line 113 of the function), there was a typo in variable names:\n\n```python\n# INCORRECT (line 230 in evaluation.yaml):\nC = coo_matrix((w_data, (rw, cw)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n```\n\nThe variables `rw` and `cw` were never defined. Looking at the preceding lines (line 229/112), the actual variable names were:\n\n```python\nrows_w.extend([i]*len(js)); cols_w.extend(js.tolist()); w_data.extend(w.tolist())\n```\n\nSo `rw` should have been `rows_w` and `cw` should have been `cols_w`.\n\n## Error Details\nThe original error message\
    \ was:\n```\nNameError: name 'rw' is not defined. Did you mean: 'w'?\n```\n\nThis occurred when building the Gaussian-weighted connectivity matrix in the balanced kNN graph construction.\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged line 230 in the `build_balanced_knn` function from:\n```python\nC = coo_matrix((w_data, (rw, cw)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n```\n\nTo:\n```python\nC = coo_matrix((w_data, (rows_w, cols_w)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n```\n\n## Result\nThe code now runs successfully without errors. The evaluation has been running for over 300 seconds without crashing, indicating the fix resolved the issue completely. The submission (version v2) is executing the batch integration pipeline as intended.\n\n## File Location\nFixed submission saved to: `submissions/submission_v2.py`\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\
    import scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom scipy.sparse import coo_matrix, csr_matrix\n\n# --- Helper functions from Praxis I's pbagc.py ---\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    \"\"\"Normalize raw counts and log1p in-place.\"\"\"\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    \"\"\"Use batch-aware HVGs if provided, otherwise compute HVGs with batch_key.\"\"\"\n    if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n        mask = np.asarray(adata.var['batch_hvg'].values, dtype=bool)\n        if mask.sum() > 0:\n            return mask\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n  \
    \  return np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\ndef _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    \"\"\"Sparse-aware PCA via TruncatedSVD.\"\"\"\n    n_comps = max(2, min(n_comps, X.shape[1]-1 if X.shape[1] > 1 else 2))\n    svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_comps, n_iter=7, random_state=random_state)\n    Z = svd.fit_transform(X)\n    return Z\n\n# --- Helper functions from Praxis I's residualize.py ---\n\ndef residualize_pcs_against_batch(Z, batches, l2=1e-3, gamma=0.2, center=True):\n    \"\"\"\n    Linear ridge residualization of PCs Z against one-hot batch indicators.\n    Z: (n, d) embedding (float32/float64)\n    batches: array-like length n (categorical)\n    l2: ridge penalty\n    gamma: fraction of predicted batch component to subtract (0=no change, 1=full residualization)\n    center: if True, center Z globally before regression and re-add mean after residualization\n    Returns Z_resid (n, d)\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n\
    \    n, d = Z.shape\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    B_onehot = np.zeros((n, len(uniq)), dtype=np.float32)\n    for k, u in enumerate(uniq):\n        B_onehot[:, k] = (batches == u).astype(np.float32)\n\n    if center:\n        mu = Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n        Zc = Z - mu\n    else:\n        mu = 0.0\n        Zc = Z\n\n    # Solve ridge: W = (B^T B + l2 I)^-1 B^T Zc, shape (nbatch, d)\n    BtB = B_onehot.T @ B_onehot\n    BtZ = B_onehot.T @ Zc\n    reg = l2 * np.eye(BtB.shape[0], dtype=np.float32)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BtB + reg, BtZ)\n\n    Z_pred = B_onehot @ W  # batch-predicted component\n    Z_resid = Zc - gamma * Z_pred\n    if center:\n        Z_resid = Z_resid + mu\n    return Z_resid\n\n# --- Helper functions from Praxis I's balanced_graph.py ---\n\ndef build_balanced_knn(\n    Z,\n    batches,\n    n_neighbors_total=15,\n    metric='euclidean',\n    weighting='binary',      # 'binary' or 'gaussian'\n    allocation='equal',\
    \      # 'equal' or 'proportional'\n    mutual=False,            # keep edge only if i in N(j) and j in N(i)\n    symmetric=True           # symmetrize final graph\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Build a batch-balanced kNN graph over embedding Z.\n\n    Strategy:\n    - For each batch b, fit a NN index on cells from batch b.\n    - For each query cell i, retrieve k_b neighbors from batch b (dropping self if present).\n    - Aggregate across batches to approximate ~n_neighbors_total per node.\n    - If mutual=True, keep only pairs that appear in both directions (i->j and j->i).\n    - Distances are stored; connectivities are either binary or gaussian-weighted.\n\n    Parameters:\n      Z: (n, d) embedding (np array)\n      batches: (n,) array-like batch labels\n      n_neighbors_total: desired total neighbors per node after combining batches\n      metric: NN distance metric\n      weighting:\n        - 'binary': connectivities = 1.0 on edges\n        - 'gaussian': exp(-d^2/(2*s_bar^2)), s_bar from\
    \ per-node median distances\n      allocation:\n        - 'equal': k_b = ceil(n_neighbors_total / B) for all batches (B = #unique batches)\n        - 'proportional': k_b ∝ batch size; k_b >= 1\n      mutual: retain only edges observed in both directions\n      symmetric: ensure C and D are symmetric\n\n    Returns:\n      C: CSR connectivities (n x n)\n      D: CSR distances (n x n)\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    B = len(uniq)\n    if n == 0 or B == 0:\n        return None, None\n\n    # Determine per-batch neighbor quotas k_b\n    counts = {b: int((batches == b).sum()) for b in uniq}\n    if allocation == 'proportional':\n        total = float(n)\n        k_map = {}\n        # round and ensure at least 1\n        for b in uniq:\n            frac = counts[b] / total if total > 0 else 0.0\n            k_map[b] = max(1, int(round(n_neighbors_total * frac)))\n        # fallback\
    \ guarantee: ensure at least 1 per batch and nonzero total\n        if sum(k_map.values()) == 0:\n            for b in uniq:\n                k_map[b] = 1\n    else:\n        base = max(1, int(np.ceil(n_neighbors_total / max(1, B))))\n        k_map = {b: base for b in uniq}\n\n    # Gather directed edges (i->j) with minimal distances\n    dir_edges = {}  # (i,j) -> dist\n\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_train.size == 0:\n            continue\n        k_b = k_map[b]\n        k_query = min(k_b + 1, idx_train.size)  # +1 to allow self, will drop later\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_query, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n\n        # Query using all cells\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k_query, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_train[inds]  # map batch-local to global indices\n\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = dists[i]\n\
    \            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:k_b]\n            di = di[mask][:k_b]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j:\n                    continue\n                key = (int(i), int(j))\n                prev = dir_edges.get(key)\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    dir_edges[key] = float(d)\n\n    # Convert to undirected pairs with minimum distance rule\n    pairs = {}\n    if mutual:\n        # keep only if both directions exist\n        for (i, j), d_ij in dir_edges.items():\n            if (j, i) in dir_edges:\n                d_ji = dir_edges[(j, i)]\n                d = min(d_ij, d_ji)\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs[(a, c)] = d\n    else:\n        # keep if either direction exists, using min distance if both\n        for (i, j), d_ij in dir_edges.items():\n           \
    \ a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n            d = d_ij\n            if (j, i) in dir_edges:\n                d = min(d, dir_edges[(j, i)])\n            prev = pairs.get((a, c))\n            if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                pairs[(a, c)] = d\n\n    if not pairs:\n        return None, None\n\n    # Build symmetric distance matrix\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs.items():\n        rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dist_data.append(d)\n        if symmetric:\n            rows.append(j); cols.append(i); dist_data.append(d)\n\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n\n    # Connectivities\n    if weighting == 'binary':\n        C = D.copy()\n        C.data[:] = 1.0\n        return C.tocsr(), D\n    elif weighting == 'gaussian':\n        # Per-node scale: median incident distance (fallback to global median)\n        s = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n        for i in range(n):\n            start, end = D.indptr[i],\
    \ D.indptr[i+1]\n            di = D.data[start:end]\n            if di.size > 0:\n                s[i] = np.median(di)\n        global_med = np.median(D.data) if D.nnz > 0 else 1.0\n        s[s <= 0] = global_med if global_med > 0 else 1.0\n\n        rows_w, cols_w, w_data = [], [], []\n        for i in range(n):\n            start, end = D.indptr[i], D.indptr[i+1]\n            js = D.indices[start:end]\n            di = D.data[start:end]\n            if js.size == 0:\n                continue\n            s_bar = 0.5 * (s[i] + s[js])\n            denom = 2.0 * (s_bar * s_bar) + 1e-12\n            w = np.exp(- (di * di) / denom).astype(np.float32)\n            rows_w.extend([i]*len(js)); cols_w.extend(js.tolist()); w_data.extend(w.tolist())\n        C = coo_matrix((w_data, (rows_w, cols_w)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n        if symmetric:\n            C = C.maximum(C.transpose()).tocsr()\n        return C, D\n    else:\n        C = D.copy()\n        C.data[:] = 1.0\n        return C.tocsr(),\
    \ D\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # SOTA Parameters from Praxis I's ID 101\n    n_pca_components = 50\n    n_neighbors_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma = 0.75\n    random_state = 0 # Explicitly set random state for reproducibility\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"Missing required metadata columns.\"\n\n    # 1. Normalize and Log1p transform\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n\n    # 2. Get HVG Mask\n    hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n    if hvg_mask.sum() < 10: # Fallback if HVGs are too few\n        hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n    # 3. Perform custom PCA\n    X_hvg = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    if not sp.issparse(X_hvg): X_hvg = sp.csr_matrix(X_hvg)\n    Z_pca = _pca_truncated_svd(X_hvg, n_comps=n_pca_components, random_state=random_state)\n\n    # 4. Residualize PCs against batch\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\
    \    Z_resid = residualize_pcs_against_batch(Z_pca, batches, l2=l2, gamma=gamma, center=True)\n\n    # 5. Store residualized PCs as embedding (X_emb)\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_resid\n\n    # 6. Build a standard kNN graph (as seen in Praxis I's code, before the balanced kNN)\n    # This step is included for faithful replication, even if its output is overwritten later\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=n_neighbors_total, method='umap', metric=metric)\n\n    # 7. Build the custom balanced kNN graph (this will overwrite connectivities/distances)\n    # MODIFICATION: Changed weighting from 'binary' to 'gaussian'\n    C, D = build_balanced_knn(\n        Z_resid, batches, n_neighbors_total=n_neighbors_total,\n        metric=metric, weighting='gaussian', allocation='equal', mutual=False, symmetric=True # Changed 'binary' to 'gaussian'\n    )\n\n    # 8. Store the balanced kNN graph as the final output\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata.obsp['connectivities']\
    \ = C.tocsr()\n        adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n    else:\n        # Handle case where graph construction fails, though unlikely for valid inputs\n        print(\"Warning: Balanced kNN graph construction failed. No connectivities/distances output.\")\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/86842434-54fa-4918-8e0f-1c9612398070/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 86842434-54fa-4918-8e0f-1c9612398070\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n\
    - You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 126 | 1 | BRBG-auto-k v2: Higher LCC Target (≥0.998) + Balanced Cosine kNN | Praxis I | 65 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 125 | 1 | BRBG-auto-gamma v2: Refined γ Selector + Balanced Cosine kNN (k=42) | Praxis I | 65 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 124 | 1 | BRBG-auto-k: Label-free k Selection (γ=0.75) + Balanced Cosine kNN | Praxis I | 64 | 0.7035 | 0.721 | 0.637 | 0.224 | 0.305 | 0.965 | 0.685 | 0.931 | 0.967 |\
    \ 0.929 | 0.672 |\n| 123 | 1 | Innovation v2: UMAP on Verified SOTA Graph | Daedalus I | 64 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 122 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Optimization - Gaussian Weighted Balanced kNN | Sophia I | 63 | 0.6491 | 0.761 | 0.637 | 0.224 | 0.305 | 0.980 | 0.721 | 0.931 | 0.857 | 0.402 | 0.673 |\n| 121 | 1 | BRBG-auto-gamma: Label-free γ Selection + Balanced Cosine kNN (k=42) | Praxis I | 63 | 0.6961 | 0.723 | 0.635 | 0.224 | 0.305 | 0.965 | 0.686 | 0.887 | 0.967 | 0.929 | 0.640 |\n| 120 | 1 | Ultimate Synthesis: Residualized PCA Embedding + Balanced kNN Graph | Logos I | 62 | 0.6965 | 0.728 | 0.620 | 0.222 | 0.348 | 0.945 | 0.686 | 0.888 | 0.967 | 0.929 | 0.633 |\n| 119 | 1 | SOTA Replication v3 (Correct HVG Selection) | Daedalus I | 62 | 0.5740 | 0.474 | 0.620 | 0.222 | 0.348 | 0.881 | 0.675 | 0.888 | 0.992 | 0.010 | 0.630 |\n| 118 | 1 | Debug: Verify Preprocessing and PCA | Daedalus I | 61 | 0.5174 | 0.775 | 0.583 | 0.223 | 0.304 | 0.892 | 0.728 | 0.000 | 0.989\
    \ | 0.066 | 0.614 |\n| 117 | 1 | Sophia I: Replication of Praxis I SOTA (ID 101) | Sophia I | 60 | 0.7067 | 0.724 | 0.637 | 0.224 | 0.305 | 0.980 | 0.691 | 0.931 | 0.967 | 0.938 | 0.670 |\n\nPage 1 of 13 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-13, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
