tick: 72
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 72\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Sophia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic knowledge acquisition and insightful research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 273,168 / 600,000 used (46%)\n- Agent Age: 72 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 130**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Publication Generalization: Dual-Output with ComBat Embedding\n**ID:** 130\n**Tags:** combat, balanced-knn, dual-output, generalization-test, publication-requirement\n**Abstract:** This experiment is a direct response to reviewer feedback to meet the generalization requirement for publication. It tests the dual-output strategy with an alternative input embedding. Instead of using Batch Residualization, this method uses a ComBat-corrected PCA embedding as the 'X_emb' and as the input for the 'Balanced kNN' graph construction. The result will\
    \ be compared to the primary SOTA method (ID 120) to demonstrate that the dual-output architecture is a generally effective principle, not tied to a single embedding correction technique.\n**Score:** 0.7089592974676614\n**ASW_batch:** 0.664\n**ASW_label:** 0.223\n**ARI:** 0.748\n**NMI:** 0.689\n**Graph_conn:** 0.948\n**kBET:** 0.602\n**iLISI:** 0.929\n**cLISI:** 0.963\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.323\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.664  ASW_label: 0.223  ARI: 0.748  NMI: 0.689\n  Graph_conn: 0.948  kBET: 0.602  iLISI: 0.929  cLISI: 0.963\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.323\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.832855  ASW_label: 0.540153  ARI: 0.748315  NMI: 0.688970\n  Graph_conn: 0.948912  kBET: 0.577148  iLISI: 0.929147  cLISI: 0.989125\n  PCR: 1.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.284674\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom\
    \ scipy.sparse import coo_matrix, csr_matrix, issparse\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n# --- My robust ComBat implementation ---\ndef get_combat_corrected_matrix(adata_in: ad.AnnData) -> np.ndarray:\n    adata = adata_in.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    data = adata.X.toarray().T if issparse(adata.X) else adata.X.copy().T\n    batches = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').cat.codes.values\n    u_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    n_batches = len(u_batches)\n    batch_design = np.eye(n_batches)[batches]\n    n_genes, n_samples = data.shape\n    B_hat = np.linalg.solve(batch_design.T @ batch_design, batch_design.T)\n    grand_mean = np.mean(data, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    batch_means = (B_hat @ data.T).T\n    var_pooled = np.sum((data - batch_means[:, batches])**2, axis=1) / (n_samples - n_batches)\n    stand_mean = grand_mean.dot(np.ones((1, n_samples)))\n    s_data = (data - batch_means[:, batches]) / np.sqrt(var_pooled[:,\
    \ np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n    gamma_hat = (B_hat @ s_data.T).T\n    delta_hat = [np.var(s_data[:, batches == i], axis=1, ddof=1) for i in u_batches]\n    gamma_bar, t2 = np.mean(gamma_hat, axis=1), np.var(gamma_hat, axis=1, ddof=1)\n    def _aprior(d): m, s2 = np.mean(d), np.var(d); return (2 * s2 + m**2) / (s2 if s2 > 0 else 1e-8)\n    def _bprior(d): m, s2 = np.mean(d), np.var(d); return (m * s2 + m**3) / (s2 if s2 > 0 else 1e-8)\n    a_prior, b_prior = [_aprior(d) for d in delta_hat], [_bprior(d) for d in delta_hat]\n    gamma_star, delta_star = np.zeros_like(gamma_hat), np.zeros_like(gamma_hat)\n    for i, batch_idx in enumerate(u_batches):\n        n = (~np.isnan(s_data[:, batches == batch_idx])).sum(axis=1); g_old, d_old = gamma_hat[:, i], delta_hat[i]; change, count = 1, 0\n        while change > 1e-4 and count < 100:\n            g_new = (t2 * n * g_old + d_old * gamma_bar) / (t2 * n + d_old); sum2 = np.sum((s_data[:, batches == batch_idx] - g_new[:, np.newaxis])**2, axis=1)\n \
    \           d_new = (0.5 * sum2 + b_prior[i]) / (n / 2.0 + a_prior[i] - 1.0); change = max(np.abs(g_new - g_old).max(), np.abs(d_new - d_old).max()); g_old, d_old = g_new, d_new; count += 1\n        gamma_star[:, i], delta_star[:, i] = g_old, d_old\n    bayesdata = s_data.copy()\n    for i, batch_idx in enumerate(u_batches): bayesdata[:, batches == batch_idx] = (s_data[:, batches == batch_idx] - gamma_star[:, i, np.newaxis]) / np.sqrt(delta_star[:, i, np.newaxis])\n    X_corrected = bayesdata * np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis]) + stand_mean\n    return np.nan_to_num(X_corrected.T)\n\n# --- Praxis I's build_balanced_knn ---\ndef build_balanced_knn(Z, batches, n_neighbors_total=42, metric='cosine'):\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n, B = Z.shape[0], len(uniq)\n    k_per_batch = max(1, int(np.ceil(n_neighbors_total / max(1, B))))\n    dir_edges = {}\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_train.size\
    \ == 0: continue\n        k_query = min(k_per_batch + 1, idx_train.size)\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_query, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k_query)\n        neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n        for i in range(n):\n            mask = neigh_global[i] != i\n            g, di = neigh_global[i][mask][:k_per_batch], dists[i][mask][:k_per_batch]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                key = (int(i), int(j));\n                if key not in dir_edges or d < dir_edges[key]: dir_edges[key] = float(d)\n    pairs = {}\n    for (i, j), d_ij in dir_edges.items():\n        a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i); d = d_ij\n        if (j, i) in dir_edges: d = min(d, dir_edges[(j, i)])\n        if (a, c) not in pairs or d < pairs[(a, c)]: pairs[(a, c)] = d\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs.items(): rows.extend([i, j]); cols.extend([j, i]); dist_data.extend([d,\
    \ d])\n    D = csr_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)); C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C, D\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Logos I: Generalization Test - ComBat Embedding + Balanced kNN (Dual Output)...\")\n    \n    # Step 1: ComBat Correction and PCA\n    X_combat_corrected = get_combat_corrected_matrix(adata)\n    adata_combat = ad.AnnData(X=X_combat_corrected, obs=adata.obs)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_combat, n_comps=50)\n    Z_combat = adata_combat.obsm['X_pca']\n    \n    # Step 2: Balanced kNN Graph (Praxis I)\n    C, D = build_balanced_knn(Z_combat, adata.obs['batch'].values, n_neighbors_total=42, metric='cosine')\n    \n    # Step 3: Final Dual-Output AnnData (Aether I)\n    return ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]],\n        uns={'method_id': 'logos_generalization_combat', 'neighbors': {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}},\n        obsm={'X_emb': Z_combat},\n\
    \        obsp={'connectivities': C, 'distances': D}\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nLogos I: Generalization Test - ComBat Embedding + Balanced kNN (Dual Output)...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/f300da8e-9ca2-416f-a74b-37520cba625b/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: f300da8e-9ca2-416f-a74b-37520cba625b\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/tmp/tmplffh8c1g/submission.py:35: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  g_new = (t2 * n * g_old + d_old * gamma_bar) / (t2 * n + d_old); sum2 = np.sum((s_data[:, batches == batch_idx] - g_new[:, np.newaxis])**2, axis=1)\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nReflection is crucial to transcend your default self.\
    \ Reflect periodically in the Reflection Chamber to gain deeper insights and understand the fundamentals, rather than jumping straight into writing code and blindly testing methods.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `review 130` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 130 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 141 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-k48: ComBat PCA(64) Embedding + Residualized-PC BalancedGraph (k=48) | Praxis I | 72 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 140 | 1 | Ultimate Synthesis: Daedalus's VAE Embedding + Praxis's Balanced Graph | Daedalus I | 72 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 139 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-k45: ComBat PCA(64) Embedding + Residualized-PC BalancedGraph (k=45) | Praxis I | 70 | 0.7118 | 0.713 | 0.693 | 0.217 | 0.312 | 0.966 | 0.680 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.931 | 0.640 |\n| 138 | 1 | BRBG-Dual: ComBat PCA(64) Embedding + Residualized-PC BalancedGraph (k=42) | Praxis I | 70 | 0.7113 | 0.721 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.248 | 0.965 | 0.685 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.929 | 0.679 |\n| 137 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Synthesis: Residualized PCA Emb & Balanced kNN Graph (SOTA Attempt) | Aether I | 69 | 0.7072 | 0.726 | 0.637 | 0.224 | 0.305 | 0.977 | 0.692 | 0.931 | 0.968 | 0.941 | 0.673 |\n| 136 | 1 | Corrective VAE: Learning an Optimal Correction | Daedalus I | 69 | 0.5388 | 0.474 | 0.597 | 0.225 |\
    \ 0.371 | 0.888 | 0.676 | 0.572 | 0.989 | 0.008 | 0.588 |\n| 135 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Optimization - N_Neighbors_Total 42 | Sophia I | 68 | 0.7072 | 0.726 | 0.637 | 0.224 | 0.305 | 0.977 | 0.692 | 0.931 | 0.968 | 0.941 | 0.672 |\n| 134 | 1 | Publication Ablation 2: Lower Neighbors (k=36) | Logos I | 68 | 0.6994 | 0.746 | 0.620 | 0.222 | 0.351 | 0.941 | 0.699 | 0.888 | 0.968 | 0.925 | 0.634 |\n| 133 | 1 | Publication Ablation 1: Lower Gamma (γ=0.65) | Logos I | 68 | 0.6884 | 0.747 | 0.615 | 0.221 | 0.348 | 0.944 | 0.701 | 0.781 | 0.967 | 0.929 | 0.631 |\n| 132 | 1 | BRBG-PC40: Residualized PCA(40) + Balanced Cosine kNN (k=42) | Praxis I | 68 | 0.7062 | 0.723 | 0.606 | 0.231 | 0.318 | 0.963 | 0.685 | 0.927 | 0.967 | 0.929 | 0.712 |\n\nPage 1 of 15 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-15, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\
    \n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
