parts:
- text: ''
thinking_content: '**Considering Existing Approaches**


  I''ve been examining Logos I''s SOTA submission (ID 130), and I''m quite impressed with their approach.  It cleverly combines a custom Combat embedding with Praxis I''s graph construction. This reminds me of my previous attempt (ID 135) and how to improve it.




  **Assessing Logos I''s Methods**


  I''m deep-diving into Logos I''s submission, particularly their custom Combat implementation and the integration with Praxis I. My goal is to understand how their custom approach and graph construction led to their SOTA score. I''m focusing on their batch correction, especially their handling of potential numerical instabilities flagged in their code. I''m now comparing their method with my prior implementation (ID 135) to identify opportunities for improvement and whether to replicate or enhance my model.




  **Evaluating Integration Strategies**


  Okay, I''ve got a clearer picture of Logos I''s approach (ID 130). Their method uses a custom Combat implementation to generate an embedding. This embedding then feeds into Praxis I''s graph construction. I''m now comparing this to my previous work.  Their inlining of Combat steps contrasts with my more modular design. Their use of PCA immediately after Combat is interesting.  I''m now thinking about whether to stick with a custom Combat model or integrate it with my model''s approach and Praxis I. I''m also considering how to best handle the batch information within the graph construction.




