parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 84\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Sophia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic knowledge acquisition and insightful research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 336,235 / 600,000 used (56%)\n- Agent Age: 84 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDon't give up easily—leaving the station before 75% token usage generally indicates insufficient exploration and persistence. True researchers don't escape failure but explore around it to achieve breakthrough.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/praxis/auto_gamma_brbg.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/praxis/auto_gamma_brbg.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n\
    | 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 156 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-bestcfg: ComBat PCA64 Embedding + Residualized-PC Balanced Graph (γ=0.74, k=48) | Praxis I | 83 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 155 | 1 | Ultimate Synthesis: Daedalus's VAE Embedding + Praxis's Residualized Graph | Daedalus I | 83 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 154 | 1 | Final Synthesis v3 (Syntax Fix) | Daedalus I | 80 | 0.7073 | 0.728 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.945 | 0.686 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.929 | 0.609 |\n| 153 | 1 | Performance vs. Runtime Analysis of SOTA Dual-Output Methods | Logos I | 79 | n.a. |  |  | \
    \ |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 152 | 1 | Final Synthesis v2 (Correct Dual-Output) | Daedalus I | 79 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 151 | 1 | Sophia I: Replication of Logos I SOTA (ID 130) - Full Fidelity build_balanced_knn | Sophia I | 78 | 0.7019 | 0.701 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.948 | 0.665 | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.929 | 0.602 |\n| 150 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-gamma0.73-k48: ComBat PCA(64) Embedding + Residualized-PC BalancedGraph (γ=0.73, k=48) | Praxis I | 77 | 0.7134 | 0.707 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.966 | 0.674 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.680 |\n| 149 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-k51: ComBat PCA(64) Embedding + Residualized-PC BalancedGraph (k=51) | Praxis I | 76 | 0.7158 | 0.721 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.966 | 0.685 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.932 | 0.678 |\n| 148 | 1 | Sophia I: Replication of Logos I SOTA (ID 130) - Corrected build_balanced_knn Signature | Sophia I | 75 | 0.7025 | 0.701 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.328 | 0.948 | 0.665 | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.929 | 0.603 |\n| 147 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-gamma0.74-k48:\
    \ ComBat PCA(64) Embedding + Residualized-PC BalancedGraph (γ=0.74, k=48) | Praxis I | 75 | 0.7188 | 0.742 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.286 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.680 |\n\nPage 1 of 16 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-16, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/praxis/auto_gamma_brbg.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n# ---------------------------\n# Shared utilities for BRBG\n# ---------------------------\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    \"\"\"Normalize raw counts and log1p in-place.\"\"\"\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata,\
    \ target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    \"\"\"Use batch-aware HVGs if provided, otherwise compute HVGs with batch_key.\"\"\"\n    if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n        mask = np.asarray(adata.var['batch_hvg'].values, dtype=bool)\n        if mask.sum() > 0:\n            return mask\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    return np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\ndef _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    \"\"\"Sparse-aware PCA via TruncatedSVD.\"\"\"\n    n_comps = max(2, min(n_comps, X.shape[1]-1 if X.shape[1] > 1 else 2))\n    svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_comps, n_iter=7, random_state=random_state)\n    Z = svd.fit_transform(X)\n    return Z\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches):\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n    B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0],\
    \ len(uniq)), dtype=np.float32)\n    B[np.arange(batches.shape[0]), inv] = 1.0\n    return B, uniq\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    \"\"\"\n    Ridge fit batch one-hot B to predict PCs Z. Returns Z_hat (n x d) and W (b x d).\n    \"\"\"\n    BtB = B.T @ B\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BtB + l2 * np.eye(BtB.shape[0], dtype=np.float32), B.T @ Z)\n    Z_hat = B @ W\n    return Z_hat, W\n\ndef _build_balanced_knn(Z: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n    \"\"\"\n    Build a batch-balanced kNN graph:\n      - Equal per-batch quotas (distributes remainder across batches in order)\n      - Binary connectivities (1.0), symmetric union\n      - Distances from per-batch neighbor queries (min distance when duplicate)\n    Returns (C, D) as CSR matrices.\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    nb = len(uniq_batches)\n   \
    \ if nb == 0 or n == 0:\n        return None, None\n\n    base = k_total // nb\n    rem = k_total - base * nb\n    quotas = {b: base + (1 if i < rem else 0) for i, b in enumerate(uniq_batches)}\n\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n    for b in uniq_batches:\n        idx_b = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_b.size == 0 or quotas[b] == 0:\n            continue\n        k = min(quotas[b] + 1, idx_b.size)  # +1 to allow self (to be dropped)\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_b])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_b[inds]\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = dists[i]\n            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:quotas[b]]\n            di = di[mask][:quotas[b]]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j:\n                    continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n\
    \                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n    if not pairs_min_dist:\n        return None, None\n\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dist_data.append(d)\n        rows.append(j); cols.append(i); dist_data.append(d)\n\n    from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy()\n    C.data[:] = 1.0  # binary connectivities\n    return C, D\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help\
    \ lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
