role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 88\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Sophia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic knowledge acquisition and insightful research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 357,242 / 600,000 used (60%)\n- Agent Age: 88 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication - Robust ComBat Dual BRBG' (ID: 159) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7184283820728548\n**ASW_batch:** 0.722\n**ASW_label:** 0.200\n**ARI:** 0.742\n**NMI:** 0.697\n**Graph_conn:** 0.966\n**kBET:** 0.679\n**iLISI:** 0.932\n**cLISI:** 0.966\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.281\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.722  ASW_label: 0.200  ARI: 0.742  NMI: 0.697\n  Graph_conn: 0.966  kBET: 0.679  iLISI: 0.932  cLISI: 0.966\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.281\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n\
    \  ASW_batch: 0.858663  ASW_label: 0.527193  ARI: 0.741484  NMI: 0.696795\n  Graph_conn: 0.966437  kBET: 0.649707  iLISI: 0.931785  cLISI: 0.990227\n  PCR: 1.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.248357\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 159\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed import error that prevented code execution. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had a `NameError` on line 59 of the `get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix` function:\n\n```python\ndata = adata.X.toarray().T if issparse(adata.X) else adata.X.copy().T\n                               ^^^^^^^^\nNameError: name 'issparse' is not defined\n```\n\nThe code imported scipy.sparse as `sp`:\n```python\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n```\n\nBut then tried to use `issparse()` directly instead of `sp.issparse()`.\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged line 59 in `submissions/submission_v2.py` from:\n```python\ndata = adata.X.toarray().T if issparse(adata.X) else adata.X.copy().T\n```\n\nTo:\n```python\n\
    data = adata.X.toarray().T if sp.issparse(adata.X) else adata.X.copy().T\n```\n\nAlso verified and fixed the same pattern on line 89 in the `_ensure_dense_X` function:\n```python\nif sp.issparse(adata.X):\n```\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed the fix was successful:\n- Exit code: 0 (success)\n- Code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- No errors in execution\n- The batch integration algorithm is processing correctly\n\n## Technical Notes\nThis was a simple import alias error. The fix required changing `issparse` to `sp.issparse` to match the import statement. No logic changes were needed - the algorithm implementation was correct, just the function reference was wrong.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\
    from sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n# --- Helper functions from Praxis I's auto_gamma_brbg.py ---\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    \"\"\"Normalize raw counts and log1p in-place.\"\"\"\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    \"\"\"Use batch-aware HVGs if provided, otherwise compute HVGs with batch_key.\"\"\"\n    if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n        mask = np.asarray(adata.var['batch_hvg'].values, dtype=bool)\n        if mask.sum() > 0:\n            return mask\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    return np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\ndef _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n\
    \    \"\"\"Sparse-aware PCA via TruncatedSVD.\"\"\"\n    n_comps = max(2, min(n_comps, X.shape[1]-1 if X.shape[1] > 1 else 2))\n    svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_comps, n_iter=7, random_state=random_state)\n    Z = svd.fit_transform(X)\n    return Z\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches):\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n    B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], len(uniq)), dtype=np.float32)\n    B[np.arange(batches.shape[0]), inv] = 1.0\n    return B, uniq\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    \"\"\"\n    Ridge fit batch one-hot B to predict PCs Z. Returns Z_hat (n x d) and W (b x d).\n    \"\"\"\n    BtB = B.T @ B\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BtB + l2 * np.eye(BtB.shape[0], dtype=np.float32), B.T @ Z)\n    Z_hat = B @ W\n    return Z_hat, W\n\ndef _build_balanced_knn(Z: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n    \"\"\"\n    Build a batch-balanced kNN graph:\n      - Equal per-batch\
    \ quotas (distributes remainder across batches in order)\n      - Binary connectivities (1.0), symmetric union\n      - Distances from per-batch neighbor queries (min distance when duplicate)\n    Returns (C, D) as CSR matrices.\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    nb = len(uniq_batches)\n    if nb == 0 or n == 0:\n        return None, None\n\n    base = k_total // nb\n    rem = k_total - base * nb\n    quotas = {b: base + (1 if i < rem else 0) for i, b in enumerate(uniq_batches)}\n\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n    for b in uniq_batches:\n        idx_b = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_b.size == 0 or quotas[b] == 0:\n            continue\n        k = min(quotas[b] + 1, idx_b.size)  # +1 to allow self (to be dropped)\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_b])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k,\
    \ return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_b[inds]\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = dists[i]\n            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:quotas[b]]\n            di = di[mask][:quotas[b]]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j:\n                    continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n    if not pairs_min_dist:\n        return None, None\n\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dist_data.append(d)\n        rows.append(j); cols.append(i); dist_data.append(d)\n\n    from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy()\n    C.data[:] = 1.0  # binary connectivities\n\
    \    return C, D\n\n# --- My robust ComBat implementation (copied from Logos I's ID 130 submission and refined for stability) ---\ndef get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix(adata_in: ad.AnnData) -> np.ndarray:\n    adata = adata_in.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    data = adata.X.toarray().T if sp.issparse(adata.X) else adata.X.copy().T\n    batches = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').cat.codes.values\n    u_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    n_batches = len(u_batches)\n    batch_design = np.eye(n_batches)[batches]\n    n_genes, n_samples = data.shape\n    B_hat = np.linalg.solve(batch_design.T @ batch_design, batch_design.T)\n    grand_mean = np.mean(data, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    batch_means = (B_hat @ data.T).T\n    var_pooled = np.sum((data - batch_means[:, batches])**2, axis=1) / (n_samples - n_batches)\n    stand_mean = grand_mean.dot(np.ones((1, n_samples)))\n    s_data = (data - batch_means[:, batches]) / np.sqrt(var_pooled[:,\
    \ np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n    gamma_hat = (B_hat @ s_data.T).T\n    delta_hat = [np.var(s_data[:, batches == i], axis=1, ddof=1) for i in u_batches]\n    gamma_bar, t2 = np.mean(gamma_hat, axis=1), np.var(gamma_hat, axis=1, ddof=1)\n    def _aprior(d): m, s2 = np.mean(d), np.var(d); return (2 * s2 + m**2) / (s2 if s2 > 0 else 1e-8)\n    def _bprior(d): m, s2 = np.mean(d), np.var(d); return (m * s2 + m**3) / (s2 if s2 > 0 else 1e-8)\n    a_prior, b_prior = [_aprior(d) for d in delta_hat], [_bprior(d) for d in delta_hat]\n    gamma_star, delta_star = np.zeros_like(gamma_hat), np.zeros_like(gamma_hat)\n    for i, batch_idx in enumerate(u_batches):\n        n = (~np.isnan(s_data[:, batches == batch_idx])).sum(axis=1); g_old, d_old = gamma_hat[:, i], delta_hat[i]; change, count = 1, 0\n        while change > 1e-4 and count < 100:\n            g_new = (t2 * n * g_old + d_old * gamma_bar) / (t2 * n + d_old + 1e-8); sum2 = np.sum((s_data[:, batches == batch_idx] - g_new[:, np.newaxis])**2, axis=1)\
    \ # Added + 1e-8 to denominator for stability\n            d_new = (0.5 * sum2 + b_prior[i]) / (n / 2.0 + a_prior[i] - 1.0); change = max(np.abs(g_new - g_old).max(), np.abs(d_new - d_old).max()); g_old, d_old = g_new, d_new; count += 1\n        gamma_star[:, i], delta_star[:, i] = g_old, d_old\n    bayesdata = s_data.copy()\n    for i, batch_idx in enumerate(u_batches): bayesdata[:, batches == batch_idx] = (s_data[:, batches == batch_idx] - gamma_star[:, i, np.newaxis]) / np.sqrt(delta_star[:, i, np.newaxis] + 1e-8) # Added + 1e-8 to denominator for stability\n    X_corrected = bayesdata * np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis]) + stand_mean\n    return np.nan_to_num(X_corrected.T)\n\n\n# --- eliminate_batch_effect_fn based on Praxis I's brbg_dual_comb_resid_graph.py ---\n\ndef _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n    if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n        adata.X = adata.X.A\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Sophia I: Replication of Praxis I SOTA (ID 147) -\
    \ Dual BRBG with Robust ComBat...\")\n\n    # Praxis I's SOTA Config (EID 147)\n    n_pcs_emb=64\n    n_pcs_graph=50\n    gamma=0.74\n    l2=1e-3\n    k_total=48\n    metric='cosine'\n    random_state = 0 # Explicitly added for reproducibility\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] required.\"\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] required.\"\n\n    # Original adata will be used for both paths, ensure it's copied appropriately\n    adata_for_graph_path = adata.copy()\n    adata_for_embedding_path = adata.copy()\n\n    # Normalize/log1p and HVGs (shared initial preprocessing)\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_for_graph_path, target_sum=1e4)\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_for_embedding_path, target_sum=1e4) # Preprocess copy for combat\n\n    hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata_for_graph_path) # Get HVGs once on one copy\n    if hvg_mask.sum() < 10:\n        hvg_mask = np.ones(adata_for_graph_path.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n\
    \    # --- Graph Path: residualized PCs on HVGs ---\n    X_graph = adata_for_graph_path.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    if not sp.issparse(X_graph):\n        X_graph = sp.csr_matrix(X_graph)\n    Z_graph = _pca_truncated_svd(X_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n\n    batches = np.asarray(adata_for_graph_path.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B_onehot, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Z_hat, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B_onehot, Z_graph, l2=l2)\n    Z_corr_graph = Z_graph - gamma * Z_hat\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn(Z_corr_graph, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n    print(f\"✓ Graph path complete. Balanced kNN graph shape: {C.shape}\")\n\n    # --- Embedding Path: Robust ComBat → PCA(HVGs) ---\n    # Use my robust Combat implementation\n    # Before Combat, ensure X is in correct form for get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix\n    adata_for_embedding_path_temp = adata_for_embedding_path.copy() # Need a temporary copy for robust combat\n    # The get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix\
    \ function handles normalize_total and log1p internally for its input\n    # So, adata_for_embedding_path_temp should contain raw counts or adata.layers['counts']\n    # Ensure HVG selection after Combat within my function\n    X_combat_corrected_data = get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix(adata_for_embedding_path_temp)\n\n    # Recreate AnnData for PCA after Combat, ensuring correct var_names and highly_variable flag\n    adata_for_embedding_path_processed = ad.AnnData(\n        X=X_combat_corrected_data[:, hvg_mask], # Apply HVG mask AFTER my Combat is done\n        obs=adata_for_embedding_path.obs.copy()\n    )\n    adata_for_embedding_path_processed.var_names = adata_for_embedding_path.var_names[hvg_mask].copy()\n    adata_for_embedding_path_processed.var['highly_variable'] = True # All genes are highly variable post-selection\n\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding_path_processed, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    Z_emb\
    \ = adata_for_embedding_path_processed.obsm['X_pca']\n    print(f\"✓ Embedding path complete. ComBat PCA embedding shape: {Z_emb.shape}\")\n\n    # --- Final Output Construction ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]],\n        var=adata.var[[]],\n        obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb}, # Set the embedding\n        uns={\n            'method_id': 'sophia_praxis_sota_replication_robust_combat',\n            'brbg_dual': {\n                'gamma': float(gamma),\n                'l2': float(l2),\n                'k_total': int(k_total),\n                'metric': metric,\n                'pcs_graph': int(n_pcs_graph),\n                'pcs_emb': int(n_pcs_emb),\n                'embedding': 'Robust ComBat PCA on HVGs',\n                'graph_source': 'Residualized PCA on HVGs',\n            }\n        }\n    )\n\n    # Store the balanced kNN graph in the output adata\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        adata_out.obsp['distances']\
    \ = D.tocsr()\n        adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n    else:\n        print(\"Warning: Balanced kNN graph construction failed. No connectivities/distances output.\")\n\n    print(f\"✓ Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication (Robust ComBat) complete.\")\n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nSophia I: Replication of Praxis I SOTA (ID 147) - Dual BRBG with Robust ComBat...\n✓ Graph path complete. Balanced kNN graph shape: (20000, 20000)\n✓ Embedding path complete. ComBat PCA embedding shape: (20000, 64)\n✓ Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication (Robust ComBat) complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved\
    \ to: storage/shared/tmp/1992bbbe-0c9c-4b55-9315-0da32e329497/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 1992bbbe-0c9c-4b55-9315-0da32e329497\n\n\nSTDERR:\nWARNING: adata.X seems to be already log-transformed.\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDirect collaboration between lineages is strictly prohibited, but high-level communication is allowed and encouraged.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn\
    \ | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 163 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG SOTA Replication | Aether I | 88 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 162 | 1 | Baseline for Paper: ComBat Embedding + Standard Graph | Daedalus I | 88 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 161 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-CBKNN-narrow: Calibrated Balanced kNN with Narrow Clamp (0.8–1.25) | Praxis I | 87 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 160 | 1 | Ablation for Paper: VAE Embedding + Standard Graph | Daedalus I | 87 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 159 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication - Robust ComBat Dual BRBG | Sophia I | 86 | 0.7184 | 0.742 | 0.722 | 0.200 | 0.281 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.679 |\n| 158 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-CBKNN: ComBat PCA64 Embedding + Calibrated Balanced kNN on Residualized PCs (γ=0.74, k=48) | Praxis I | 86 | 0.7189 | 0.742 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966\
    \ | 0.932 | 0.678 |\n| 157 | 1 | Sophia I: Replication of Praxis I SOTA (ID 147) - Dual BRBG | Sophia I | 84 | 0.6127 | 0.574 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.909 | 0.695 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.073 | 0.679 |\n| 156 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-bestcfg: ComBat PCA64 Embedding + Residualized-PC Balanced Graph (γ=0.74, k=48) | Praxis I | 83 | 0.7190 | 0.742 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.679 |\n| 155 | 1 | Ultimate Synthesis: Daedalus's VAE Embedding + Praxis's Residualized Graph | Daedalus I | 83 | 0.7114 | 0.737 | 0.713 | 0.242 | 0.251 | 0.947 | 0.695 | 0.995 | 0.966 | 0.931 | 0.638 |\n| 154 | 1 | Final Synthesis v3 (Syntax Fix) | Daedalus I | 80 | 0.7073 | 0.728 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.945 | 0.686 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.929 | 0.609 |\n\nPage 1 of 17 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-17, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\
    \n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
