role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 100\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Sophia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic knowledge acquisition and insightful research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 426,370 / 600,000 used (71%)\n- Agent Age: 100 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 161**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** BRBG-Dual-CBKNN-narrow: Calibrated Balanced kNN with Narrow Clamp (0.8–1.25)\n**ID:** 161\n**Tags:** dual, combat, residualization, balanced-knn, calibration, cosine\n**Abstract:** Dual-output (ComBat PCA64 embedding) with residualized-PC graph (γ=0.74, l2=1e-3, k=48). CBKNN uses equal per-batch quotas with per-batch distance rescaling from within-batch medians, but with a narrower clamp (0.8–1.25) and k_calib=24 to avoid over-correction.\n**Score:** 0.719032575913731\n**ASW_batch:** 0.703\n**ASW_label:** 0.217\n**ARI:** 0.742\n**NMI:** 0.697\n\
    **Graph_conn:** 0.966\n**kBET:** 0.679\n**iLISI:** 0.932\n**cLISI:** 0.966\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.289\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.703  ASW_label: 0.217  ARI: 0.742  NMI: 0.697\n  Graph_conn: 0.966  kBET: 0.679  iLISI: 0.932  cLISI: 0.966\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.289\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.850049  ASW_label: 0.536976  ARI: 0.741484  NMI: 0.696795\n  Graph_conn: 0.966437  kBET: 0.649353  iLISI: 0.931785  cLISI: 0.990227\n  PCR: 0.999957  Cell_cycle: 0.255736\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage')\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\nfrom praxis.auto_gamma_brbg import (\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace,\n    _get_hvg_mask,\n    _pca_truncated_svd,\n    _one_hot_batches,\n    _ridge_batch_fit_predict,\n)\nfrom praxis.cbknn import build_balanced_knn_calibrated\n\ndef _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n\
    \    if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n        adata.X = adata.X.A\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Base config (best-known dual)\n    n_pcs_emb = 64\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    gamma = 0.74\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    # CBKNN ablation params\n    k_calib = 24\n    clamp = (0.8, 1.25)\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize + HVGs\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n    if hvg_mask.sum() < 10:\n        hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n    # Residualized PCs (graph source)\n    X = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    if not sp.issparse(X):\n        X = sp.csr_matrix(X)\n    Z = _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Z_hat, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n\
    \    Z_corr = Z - gamma * Z_hat\n\n    # Calibrated balanced kNN\n    C, D = build_balanced_knn_calibrated(Z_corr, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric, k_calib=k_calib, clamp=clamp)\n\n    # Embedding: ComBat PCA on HVGs\n    _ensure_dense_X(adata)\n    sc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')\n    adata.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask\n    sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.obsm['X_pca']\n\n    # Initialize neighbors then override with calibrated graph\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn,\
    \ executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nFound 33 genes with zero variance.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/95bf1005-6cd3-44a3-b422-b3f1b16ebaca/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 95bf1005-6cd3-44a3-b422-b3f1b16ebaca\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nExplicitly state your identity, current location, and a brief recap of recent events at the beginning of each response. Always include a verbose,\
    \ general reflection on past events and future plans.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `review 161` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 161 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 177 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-PCWeight: Batch R^2-based PC Weighting for Residualized Graph | Praxis I | 99 | running\
    \ |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 176 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-gPC56: Residualized Graph with 56 PCs + ComBat PCA64 Embedding | Praxis I | 97 | 0.7041 | 0.639 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.967 | 0.650 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.678 |\n| 175 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication - Dual BRBG (sc.pp.combat for Embedding Path - ASW_label Fix ... | Sophia I | 95 | 0.7188 | 0.742 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.286 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.680 |\n| 174 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-RobustLocComBat: Location-only Robust ComBat Embedding + Residualized Balanced Graph | Praxis I | 95 | 0.6057 | 0.742 | 0.618 | 0.216 | 0.271 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 0.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.650 |\n| 173 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication - Robust ComBat Dual BRBG - Full Gene Combat (ASW_label Fix) | Sophia I | 93 | 0.7148 | 0.742 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.243 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.684 |\n| 172 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-RobustMADComBat-cons: Conservative Robust MAD ComBat (clamp 0.5–2.0) | Praxis I | 93 | 0.6094 |\
    \ 0.742 | 0.621 | 0.215 | 0.316 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 0.026 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.613 |\n| 171 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-RobustMADComBat: Robust MAD-based ComBat Embedding + Residualized Balanced Graph | Praxis I | 92 | 0.6036 | 0.742 | 0.620 | 0.213 | 0.296 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 0.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.605 |\n| 170 | 1 | Generalization for Paper: Higher Neighbors (k=51) | Daedalus I | 92 | 0.7112 | 0.736 | 0.713 | 0.242 | 0.251 | 0.947 | 0.694 | 0.995 | 0.964 | 0.932 | 0.639 |\n| 169 | 1 | Generalization for Paper: Lower Gamma (0.70) | Daedalus I | 91 | 0.7131 | 0.747 | 0.713 | 0.242 | 0.251 | 0.946 | 0.702 | 0.995 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.638 |\n| 168 | 1 | Separation Analysis: ComBat PCA64 vs Residualized PC50 (Angles, Batch R^2, Overlap) | Praxis I | 90 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nPage 1 of 18 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-18, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter\
    \ tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
