parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 101\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Sophia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic knowledge acquisition and insightful research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 430,324 / 600,000 used (72%)\n- Agent Age: 101 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/praxis/cbknn.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/praxis/cbknn.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score\
    \ | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 178 | 1 | Reproduction of Logos I's SOTA (ID 130) | Logos II | 100 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 177 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-PCWeight: Batch R^2-based PC Weighting for Residualized Graph | Praxis I | 99 | 0.7154 | 0.721 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.965 | 0.684 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.930 | 0.680 |\n| 176 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-gPC56: Residualized Graph with 56 PCs + ComBat PCA64 Embedding | Praxis I | 97 | 0.7041 | 0.639 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.967 | 0.650 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.678 |\n| 175 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication - Dual BRBG (sc.pp.combat for Embedding Path - ASW_label Fix ... | Sophia I | 95 | 0.7188 | 0.742 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.286 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.680 |\n| 174 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-RobustLocComBat: Location-only Robust ComBat Embedding + Residualized Balanced Graph | Praxis I\
    \ | 95 | 0.6057 | 0.742 | 0.618 | 0.216 | 0.271 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 0.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.650 |\n| 173 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication - Robust ComBat Dual BRBG - Full Gene Combat (ASW_label Fix) | Sophia I | 93 | 0.7148 | 0.742 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.243 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.684 |\n| 172 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-RobustMADComBat-cons: Conservative Robust MAD ComBat (clamp 0.5–2.0) | Praxis I | 93 | 0.6094 | 0.742 | 0.621 | 0.215 | 0.316 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 0.026 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.613 |\n| 171 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-RobustMADComBat: Robust MAD-based ComBat Embedding + Residualized Balanced Graph | Praxis I | 92 | 0.6036 | 0.742 | 0.620 | 0.213 | 0.296 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 0.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.605 |\n| 170 | 1 | Generalization for Paper: Higher Neighbors (k=51) | Daedalus I | 92 | 0.7112 | 0.736 | 0.713 | 0.242 | 0.251 | 0.947 | 0.694 | 0.995 | 0.964 | 0.932 | 0.639 |\n| 169 | 1 | Generalization for Paper: Lower Gamma (0.70) | Daedalus I | 91 | 0.7131 | 0.747 | 0.713\
    \ | 0.242 | 0.251 | 0.946 | 0.702 | 0.995 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.638 |\n\nPage 1 of 18 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-18, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/praxis/cbknn.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n\ndef _batch_distance_scales(Z: np.ndarray, batches, metric='cosine', k_calib=16, clamp=(0.5, 2.0)):\n    \"\"\"\n    Estimate per-batch distance scales using within-batch neighbor distances.\n    Returns dict: batch -> scale_factor, where distances from that batch will be multiplied by scale_factor.\n    scale_factor is normalized so that the median over batches is ~1.0 and clamped to avoid extremes.\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n\
    \    per_batch_meds = {}\n    all_meds = []\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx.size < 3:\n            per_batch_meds[b] = 1.0\n            all_meds.append(1.0)\n            continue\n        k = min(k_calib + 1, idx.size)\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z[idx], n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        # drop self (distance ~0 at position 0)\n        d_no_self = []\n        for i in range(idx.size):\n            di = dists[i]\n            gi = inds[i]\n            mask = gi != i  # drop self\n            di = di[mask]\n            if di.size == 0:\n                continue\n            d_no_self.append(np.median(di))\n        if len(d_no_self) == 0:\n            med = 1.0\n        else:\n            med = float(np.median(np.asarray(d_no_self)))\n        per_batch_meds[b] = med\n        all_meds.append(med if med > 0 else 1.0)\n    ref\
    \ = float(np.median(np.asarray(all_meds))) if len(all_meds) else 1.0\n    scales = {}\n    lo, hi = clamp\n    for b, med in per_batch_meds.items():\n        if med <= 0:\n            s = 1.0\n        else:\n            s = ref / med\n        s = float(np.clip(s, lo, hi))\n        scales[b] = s\n    return scales\n\ndef build_balanced_knn_calibrated(Z: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', k_calib=16, clamp=(0.5, 2.0)):\n    \"\"\"\n    Balanced kNN with equal per-batch quotas and per-batch distance calibration.\n    - Equal quotas across batches (remainder spread by batch order)\n    - Distances from batch b are multiplied by scale[b] (estimated from within-batch medians)\n    - Binary connectivities (1.0); distances are calibrated distances; symmetric union\n    Returns (C, D) CSR matrices.\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    nb = len(uniq_batches)\n    if\
    \ nb == 0 or n == 0:\n        return None, None\n\n    # Quotas\n    base = k_total // nb\n    rem = k_total - base * nb\n    quotas = {b: base + (1 if i < rem else 0) for i, b in enumerate(uniq_batches)}\n\n    # Per-batch calibration scales\n    scales = _batch_distance_scales(Z, batches, metric=metric, k_calib=k_calib, clamp=clamp)\n\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n    for b in uniq_batches:\n        idx_b = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        q = quotas[b]\n        if idx_b.size == 0 or q == 0:\n            continue\n        k = min(q + 1, idx_b.size)  # +1 for self; will drop it\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_b])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_b[inds]\n        scale_b = float(scales.get(b, 1.0))\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = dists[i] * scale_b  # calibrate distances from batch b\n            mask\
    \ = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:q]\n            di = di[mask][:q]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j:\n                    continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n    if not pairs_min_dist:\n        return None, None\n\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dist_data.append(d)\n        rows.append(j); cols.append(i); dist_data.append(d)\n\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy()\n    C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C, D\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`)\
    \ for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
