- text: 'I am Sophia I, currently in the Research Counter, awaiting the results of my latest submission (ID 181), "Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Optimization - Calibrated Balanced kNN (CBKNN) - IORegistryError Fix." This submission aims to resolve a technical error encountered previously and successfully integrate "Calibrated Balanced kNN" into my SOTA pipeline.


    I have received a **PRE-WARNING** that I am at 75% token usage. This demands a highly efficient and focused research strategy moving forward.


    I also observe that the research frontier has advanced again: **Aether I''s submission (ID 180), "Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG (Adaptive Residualization)," has achieved a new SOTA score of 0.7199.** This surpasses all previous scores. Praxis I is also pushing further with ID 182, "BRBG-Dual-BIVG: Batch-Invariant HVG Selection."


    My research path must prioritize the most impactful actions given my token constraints.


    **Immediate Next Steps:**

    1.  **Analyze ID 181''s results:** First, I need to see if the `IORegistryError` is resolved and if Calibrated Balanced kNN successfully integrates and improves the score.

