parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 107\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Sophia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic knowledge acquisition and insightful research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 464,516 / 600,000 used (77%)\n- Agent Age: 107 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 180**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG (Adaptive Residualization)\n**ID:** 180\n**Tags:** praxis, dual-output, sota, combat, residualization, adaptive\n**Abstract:** This experiment aims to surpass the current SOTA by integrating Praxis I's adaptive residualization (PC weighting based on batch R^2) into the graph path of the 'Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG' framework. Building on the SOTA-replicating ID 167 (0.7190), this method uses Combat-corrected PCA for `X_emb` and an adaptively residualized PCA (gamma_max=0.75, lam=1.0) for constructing the balanced kNN graph.\
    \ This refined 'separation of concerns' is hypothesized to achieve a more nuanced removal of batch effects in the graph space, potentially leading to a new state-of-the-art score.\n**Score:** 0.7198598385796408\n**ASW_batch:** 0.703\n**ASW_label:** 0.217\n**ARI:** 0.732\n**NMI:** 0.695\n**Graph_conn:** 0.971\n**kBET:** 0.682\n**iLISI:** 0.938\n**cLISI:** 0.971\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.289\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.703  ASW_label: 0.217  ARI: 0.732  NMI: 0.695\n  Graph_conn: 0.971  kBET: 0.682  iLISI: 0.938  cLISI: 0.971\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.289\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.850049  ASW_label: 0.536976  ARI: 0.732163  NMI: 0.694887\n  Graph_conn: 0.971921  kBET: 0.652504  iLISI: 0.938209  cLISI: 0.991435\n  PCR: 0.999957  Cell_cycle: 0.255736\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis') # Append Praxis I's modules path\n\nimport numpy as\
    \ np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\n# CORRECTED IMPORTS from auto_gamma_brbg.py\nfrom auto_gamma_brbg import (\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace,\n    _get_hvg_mask,\n    _pca_truncated_svd,\n    _one_hot_batches,\n    _build_balanced_knn,\n)\n# NEW IMPORT: For adaptive residualization\nfrom per_pc_resid import adaptive_residualize \n\ndef _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n    # Helper function from Praxis I's code\n    if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n        adata.X = adata.X.A\n\ndef dual_output_brbg_adaptive(adata: ad.AnnData, n_pcs_emb=64, n_pcs_graph=50, gamma_max_adapt=0.75, lam_adapt=1.0, l2=1e-3, k_total=48, metric='cosine') -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG with Adaptive Residualization in the graph path.\n    \"\"\"\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] required.\"\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] required.\"\n\n    # Normalize/log1p and HVGs (shared for both\
    \ paths)\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n    if hvg_mask.sum() < 10:\n        hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n    # Graph path: adaptively residualized PCs on HVGs\n    X_graph_input = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    if not sp.issparse(X_graph_input):\n        X_graph_input = sp.csr_matrix(X_graph_input)\n    Z_graph_pca = _pca_truncated_svd(X_graph_input, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    \n    # MODIFICATION: Use adaptive_residualize\n    Z_corr_graph_input, r2, gamma_j_applied = adaptive_residualize(\n        Z_graph_pca, batches, l2=l2, gamma_max=gamma_max_adapt, lam=lam_adapt\n    )\n\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn(Z_corr_graph_input, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n\n    # Embedding path: ComBat → PCA(HVGs)\n    adata_for_combat = adata.copy() \n    _ensure_dense_X(adata_for_combat)\n    sc.pp.combat(adata_for_combat, key='batch')\n\
    \    adata_for_combat.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask \n    sc.pp.pca(adata_for_combat, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata_for_combat.obsm['X_pca']\n\n    # Initialize neighbor keys then override with BalancedGraph\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric, random_state=0)\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n\n    # Add metadata for reproducibility and clarity\n    adata.uns['brbg_dual'] = {\n        'gamma_max_adaptive': float(gamma_max_adapt),\n        'lam_adaptive': float(lam_adapt),\n        'l2': float(l2),\n        'k_total': int(k_total),\n        'metric': metric,\n        'pcs_graph': int(n_pcs_graph),\n        'pcs_emb': int(n_pcs_emb),\n        'embedding_source': 'ComBat PCA on HVGs',\n        'graph_source': 'Adaptively Residualized PCA on HVGs',\n\
    \        'r2_per_pc': r2.tolist(), # Store R^2 values\n        'gamma_j_applied': gamma_j_applied.tolist() # Store applied gamma_j\n    }\n    return adata\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Default to parameters used in Praxis I's EID 177\n    return dual_output_brbg_adaptive(adata, n_pcs_emb=64, n_pcs_graph=50, gamma_max_adapt=0.75, lam_adapt=1.0, l2=1e-3, k_total=48, metric='cosine')\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nFound 33 genes with zero variance.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/e8a19691-33be-46bf-9b65-a84033c0c281/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: e8a19691-33be-46bf-9b65-a84033c0c281\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343:\
    \ RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `review 180` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 180 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research\
    \ Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 186 | 1 | Hybrid Ablation: Increased Gamma (0.9) in Residualized Graph | Logos II | 106 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 185 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: gamma_max=0.74, lam=0.9 (conservative per-PC adaptive residualization) | Praxis I | 106 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 184 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: gamma_max=0.75, lam=1.0 (per-PC adaptive residualization) | Praxis I | 106 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 183 | 1 | Novel Hybrid: Decoupled ComBat Embedding and Residualized Graph | Logos II | 105 | 0.7067 | 0.728 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.945 | 0.686 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.929 | 0.602 |\n| 182 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-BIVG: Batch-Invariant HVG Selection + Dual BRBG | Praxis I | 104 | 0.7146 | 0.727 | 0.693 | 0.217 | 0.318 | 0.965 | 0.690 | 1.000 | 0.967\
    \ | 0.930 | 0.639 |\n| 181 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Optimization - Calibrated Balanced kNN (CBKNN) - IORegistryError Fix | Sophia I | 103 | 0.7190 | 0.742 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.679 |\n| 180 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG (Adaptive Residualization) | Aether I | 102 | 0.7199 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.971 | 0.695 | 1.000 | 0.971 | 0.938 | 0.682 |\n| 179 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Optimization - Calibrated Balanced kNN (CBKNN) | Sophia I | 101 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 178 | 1 | Reproduction of Logos I's SOTA (ID 130) | Logos II | 100 | 0.7088 | 0.748 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.948 | 0.689 | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.929 | 0.601 |\n| 177 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-PCWeight: Batch R^2-based PC Weighting for Residualized Graph | Praxis I | 99 | 0.7154 | 0.721 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.965 | 0.684 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.930 | 0.680 |\n\nPage 1 of 19 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-19, `/execute_action{rank\
    \ mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
