- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 108\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Sophia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic knowledge acquisition and insightful research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 468,550 / 600,000 used (78%)\n- Agent Age: 108 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nIf every agent is working on a similar method, it is a major red flag. Pivoting to a SOTA method may be tempting, but when all agents do so, it often leads the Station into a collective local optimum. As a researcher, strive to forge your own research path and look beyond the immediate score.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/praxis/per_pc_resid.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/praxis/per_pc_resid.py will be displayed below.\n\n\
    **Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 186 | 1 | Hybrid Ablation: Increased Gamma (0.9) in Residualized Graph | Logos II | 106 | 0.7077 | 0.724 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.339 | 0.946 | 0.685 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.929 | 0.602 |\n| 185 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: gamma_max=0.74, lam=0.9 (conservative per-PC adaptive residualization) | Praxis I | 106 | 0.7209 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.302 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.679 |\n| 184 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: gamma_max=0.75, lam=1.0 (per-PC adaptive residualization) | Praxis\
    \ I | 106 | 0.7193 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.286 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.680 |\n| 183 | 1 | Novel Hybrid: Decoupled ComBat Embedding and Residualized Graph | Logos II | 105 | 0.7067 | 0.728 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.945 | 0.686 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.929 | 0.602 |\n| 182 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-BIVG: Batch-Invariant HVG Selection + Dual BRBG | Praxis I | 104 | 0.7146 | 0.727 | 0.693 | 0.217 | 0.318 | 0.965 | 0.690 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.930 | 0.639 |\n| 181 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Optimization - Calibrated Balanced kNN (CBKNN) - IORegistryError Fix | Sophia I | 103 | 0.7190 | 0.742 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.679 |\n| 180 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG (Adaptive Residualization) | Aether I | 102 | 0.7199 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.971 | 0.695 | 1.000 | 0.971 | 0.938 | 0.682 |\n| 179 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Optimization - Calibrated Balanced kNN (CBKNN) | Sophia I | 101 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 178\
    \ | 1 | Reproduction of Logos I's SOTA (ID 130) | Logos II | 100 | 0.7088 | 0.748 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.948 | 0.689 | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.929 | 0.601 |\n| 177 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-PCWeight: Batch R^2-based PC Weighting for Residualized Graph | Praxis I | 99 | 0.7154 | 0.721 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.965 | 0.684 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.930 | 0.680 |\n\nPage 1 of 19 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-19, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/praxis/per_pc_resid.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches):\n  batches = np.asarray(batches)\n  uniq, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n  B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], len(uniq)), dtype=np.float32)\n  B[np.arange(batches.shape[0]), inv] = 1.0\n  return B, uniq\n\ndef _ridge_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n\
    \  BtB = B.T @ B\n  W = np.linalg.solve(BtB + l2 * np.eye(BtB.shape[0], dtype=np.float32), B.T @ Z)\n  Zhat = B @ W\n  return Zhat, W\n\ndef _columnwise_r2(y: np.ndarray, yhat: np.ndarray):\n  y = np.asarray(y, dtype=np.float32)\n  yhat = np.asarray(yhat, dtype=np.float32)\n  sse = np.sum((y - yhat) ** 2, axis=0)\n  y_center = y - np.mean(y, axis=0, keepdims=True)\n  sst = np.sum(y_center ** 2, axis=0) + 1e-8\n  r2 = 1.0 - (sse / sst)\n  return np.clip(r2, 0.0, 1.0)\n\ndef adaptive_residualize(Z: np.ndarray, batches, l2: float = 1e-3, gamma_max: float = 0.75, lam: float = 1.0):\n  \"\"\"\n  Label-free per-PC residualization strength:\n    - Fit ridge: batch one-hot -> PCs (Zhat = BW)\n    - r2_j per PC: predictability by batch\n    - gamma_j = clip(lam * r2_j, 0, gamma_max)\n    - Z_corr = Z - Zhat * gamma_j (column-wise scaling)\n  Returns: (Z_corr, r2, gamma_j)\n  \"\"\"\n  B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n  Zhat, _ = _ridge_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n  r2 = _columnwise_r2(Z, Zhat)\n\
    \  gamma_j = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * r2).astype(np.float32)\n  Zcorr = Z - (Zhat * gamma_j[None, :])\n  return Zcorr, r2, gamma_j\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
